p,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff037c388-86a0-493a-80be-03afaf174024_1100x761.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!cF0k!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff037c388-86a0-493a-80be-03afaf174024_1100x761.png\" width=\"1100\" height=\"761\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/f037c388-86a0-493a-80be-03afaf174024_1100x761.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:761,&quot;width&quot;:1100,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:null,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;Take A Pause Live community on Insight Timer with Erin Lee&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Take A Pause Live community on Insight Timer with Erin Lee&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:null,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"Take A Pause Live community on Insight Timer with Erin Lee\" title=\"Take A Pause Live community on Insight Timer with Erin Lee\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!cF0k!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff037c388-86a0-493a-80be-03afaf174024_1100x761.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!cF0k!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff037c388-86a0-493a-80be-03afaf174024_1100x761.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!cF0k!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff037c388-86a0-493a-80be-03afaf174024_1100x761.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!cF0k!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff037c388-86a0-493a-80be-03afaf174024_1100x761.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><blockquote><p><strong>Saturdays 7:30 AM Singapore Time</strong></p><p><strong>Sundays 9:00 PM Singapore Time</strong></p></blockquote><p>Sometimes all we need is a pause, to understand how to live better.</p><p>Initiated by Mindfulness Coach Erin Lee, we keep the spirit of Take A Pause intentionally simple: gathering at the end of each week, paying attention together, sharing a short reading, and reflecting on a key teaching to carry into the days ahead.​</p><p>We are a community not because of structure or formality, but because we show up—for ourselves and for one another—and become quiet accountability partners on this path of mindful living.</p><p>All are welcome to join!</p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://insighttimer.com/erinmindfulmoments/events&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Join Take A Pause Live&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:&quot;button-wrapper&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary button-wrapper\" href=\"https://insighttimer.com/erinmindfulmoments/events\"><span>Join Take A Pause Live</span></a></p>",
  "body_text": "It is easy to want a calmer mind and then become impatient with the effort involved. \n\nWe sit down to meditate, encounter the familiar distraction or drowsiness, and wonder whether anything is really changing. The wish for progress can itself become a hindrance. \n\nIn the Nava Sutta, the Buddha describes a hen caring for her eggs. Wishing for them to hatch is insufficient; she must provide warmth and proper incubation. The teaching invites us to consider the conditions we create for our own development. If we want to grow, we have to create the conditions that support our growth.\n\nOur practice can draw on four qualities associated with the four bases of power: aspiration, energy, intent, and investigation. Applied to everyday practice, these offer practical guidance:\n\n(1) Remember why we practise. \n(2) Make the effort sustainable. \n(3) Give it our attention and will. \n(4) Examine what helps or doesn’t, and adjust accordingly.\n\nThis might mean putting the phone aside, asking for twenty uninterrupted minutes, or choosing a time when we are more alert. If evening meditation repeatedly ends in drowsiness, trying the morning is a useful experiment. If we miss a day, begin again. Curiosity makes it easier to learn from these experiences without turning them into judgments about ourselves.\n\nThe same sutta describes a carpenter whose tool handle gradually wears down through daily use. The incremental change is difficult to measure, yet its cumulative effect becomes apparent. This offers a helpful perspective when we feel compelled to assess every meditation session.\n\nDuring a meditation like the body scan, this work is quiet and straightforward: notice sensations, recognise when attention has wandered, and return. Each return is an opportunity to practise patience and attention. Each practice creates the conditions for the transformation we want to see. \n\n---\n\nOver 10 and 11 October, the Take A Pause community reflected on “the quiet work of change” and patiently practiced the body scan together. We closed the session with the reading of the poem “The Seedling” by Paul Laurence Dunbar. \n\nTap Play to Meditate:\n\nThis post is free for some time, and then archived for paid subscribers to support a sustainable, long-term sharing of mindful content. To support Erin’s work, upgrade to receive lifetime access to the full archive and ongoing updates.\n\nShare\n\n---\n\nJoin Erin at Take A Pause Live\n\nSaturdays 7:30 AM Singapore Time\n\nSundays 9:00 PM Singapore Time\n\nSometimes all we need is a pause, to understand how to live better.\n\nInitiated by Mindfulness Coach Erin Lee, we keep the spirit of Take A Pause intentionally simple: gathering at the end of each week, paying attention together, sharing a short reading, and reflecting on a key teaching to carry into the days ahead.​\n\nWe are a community not because of structure or formality, but because we show up—for ourselves and for one another—and become quiet accountability partners on this path of mindful living.\n\nAll are welcome to join!\n\nJoin Take A Pause Live",
